  "economy": {
    "canonical_prices": [],
    "price_claims": [
      {
        "text": "Central Continent learns that guts Gu can leave Dang Hun Mountain and be stored, so they can be traded. Fang Yuan begins selling them after souls are fed into the mountain to form new batches. The text also calls guts Gu consumable: gone after one use. Fang Yuan holds a monopoly on the guts Gu market, choosing his buyers and setting how much he sells.",
        "chapters": [
          707
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "trade-and-storage",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "reg_central_continent"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "game_proposals": []
  },
  "distribution": {
    "locations": [],
    "factions": [],
    "origin": "unknown",
    "claims": []
  },
  "ownership_history": [
    {
      "character": "char_fang_yuan",
      "role": "user",
      "recorded_chapter": 410,
      "from_chapter": null,
      "to_chapter": null,
      "confidence": "B",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu"
    }
  ],
  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan first meets this Gu on Dang Hun Mountain inside Hu Immortal blessed land. When he smashes a gutstone, a Gu flies out, turns into a grey eerie light, and enters his body. His mind clears, strength enters his soul, and the buzzing in his ears lessens.",
        "chapters": [
          410
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "loc_dang_hun_mountain",
          "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Souls of living beings break on Dang Hun Mountain, scatter, and fuse with it. Over time gutstones form, and some of those gutstones hold guts Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          410
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Not every gutstone contains one.",
        "chapters": [
          411
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the early Hu Immortal stretch the text says guts Gu lasts only an instant after it appears, then disperses or is broken down by the mountain again. Gutstones cannot be moved, so the Gu must be used on the spot.",
        "chapters": [
          410
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fairy_bai_hu",
          "res_gutstones"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Later production still depends on souls. Guts Gu does not appear from nothing; it requires souls.",
        "chapters": [
          1502
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "On a repaired Dang Hun Mountain, Fang Yuan runs a soul path formation that spends soul beasts and soul cores so guts Gu form in huge batches.",
        "chapters": [
          1792
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "production",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Introducing Dang Hun Mountain, this Legends of Ren Zu episode follows: Wisdom Gu tells Ren Zu that to climb past Dang Hun Mountain he must smash gutstones and gain guts Gu’s help.",
        "chapters": [
          410
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "in-the-ren-zu-legend",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_the_legends_of_ren_zu",
          "gu_wisdom_gu",
          "char_ren_zu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In the telling that follows, Ren Zu picks guts Gu there, his soul strengthens, and he can endure the mountain’s tremors well enough to pass.",
        "chapters": [
          411
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "in-the-ren-zu-legend",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Evaluating a newly devised immortal material, star night mucus, Fang Yuan judges that in the short run its value and profit would rival guts Gu’s.",
        "chapters": [
          931
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "compared-to-a-new-rival",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "While recovering from Luo Po Valley, Fang Yuan consumes guts Gu again. The narration calls guts Gu a mortal Gu and says healing soul injuries with it shows instant effects.",
        "chapters": [
          997
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-gu-label",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_luo_po_valley",
          "sys_mortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "While managing his immortal aperture in Lang Ya blessed land, Fang Yuan enters Luo Po Valley every day to temper his soul, then uses guts Gu afterward to heal and strengthen it.",
        "chapters": [
          1084
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-gu-label",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Formed from a secluded domain of heaven and earth, it is a mortal Gu whose soul strengthening can affect even Gu Immortals.",
        "chapters": [
          1792
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "mortal-gu-label",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Rockmen desire guts Gu more than humans do, since it is the best way to grow and develop a rockman tribe.",
        "chapters": [
          1146
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "best-way-to-grow-rockmen",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After capturing Ye Lui Qun Xing’s corpse and sealing his soul, Fang Yuan uses many guts Gu to pull the soul back from the verge of dissipation. The narration calls guts Gu one of the world’s best methods of soul strengthening despite being only a mortal Gu, because it was created from a secluded domain of heaven and earth.",
        "chapters": [
          1206
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "saving-anothers-soul",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ye_lui_qun_xing"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Taking Jing Miao Zi’s aptitude test inside Sea Calming Lord’s dream realm, Fang Yuan can fall into the pool seventeen to eighteen times on each entry before his soul reaches its limit, and then uses guts Gu to heal himself.",
        "chapters": [
          1247
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-through-a-water-path-trial",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "It is only a mortal Gu, but coming from Dang Hun Mountain puts it beyond ordinary. When Ying Wu Xie’s Soul Howl hits Fang Yuan, a soul injury does not matter to him, because he has guts Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1257
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "beyond-ordinary-despite-being-mortal",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ying_wu_xie"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When Fang Yuan’s attempt to explore a dream realm fails and injures his soul, he crushes two guts Gu in succession and the injury heals completely. He names guts Gu one of his two advantages for exploring dream realms, since it heals the soul that exploration injures. Wanting a large personal supply for further exploration, he stops selling his portion of guts Gu for profit and accumulates it instead, and the resulting drop in income leads him to expand his other resource businesses.",
        "chapters": [
          1324
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "dream-realm-exploration",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Guts Gu’s production is limited by the quality and quantity of souls available. Lang Ya Sect supplies it by killing desolate beasts in Tai Qiu for their souls, replenished by souls brought in from treasure yellow heaven and the northern icy plain.",
        "chapters": [
          1327
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "killing-desolate-beasts-for-souls",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_lang_ya_sect",
          "loc_tai_qiu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Guts Gu protects Fang Yuan’s soul, but the soul still turns agitated when he works it too hard, and guts Gu cannot resolve that; only sleep restores its calm.",
        "chapters": [
          1328
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "cannot-calm-an-overworked-soul",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Dang Hun Mountain and Luo Po Valley are filled with soul path dao marks. The text says guts Gu and Luo Po winds are in essence adding soul path dao marks to Fang Yuan’s soul.",
        "chapters": [
          1482
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "soul-path-dao-marks",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Weighing which variant human race to raise in City Well, Fang Yuan recalls that guts Gu let him raise a batch of rockmen before, and would let him do so again very easily.",
        "chapters": [
          1489
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
